om/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T10:58:50Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T10:59:26Z","body":"This is not a bug, see the documentation:\n> Returns a `Rect2` representing the Sprite2D's boundary in local coordinates.\n\nThat means it doesn't consider any transformations, and changing this would break compatibility","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3056935297/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057150094","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108447#issuecomment-3057150094","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108447","id":3057150094,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62OGiO","user":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-10T11:59:50Z","updated_at":"2025-07-10T11:59:50Z","body":"> This is not a bug, see the documentation:\n> \n> > Returns a `Rect2` representing the Sprite2D's boundary in local coordinates.\n> \n> That means it doesn't consider any transformations, and changing this would break compatibility\n\nI can't understand that why can  'the Sprite2D's boundary in local coordinates' means it doesn't consider any transformations. The modified scale it's itself's, not it's parent node's. This is not intuitive that if the user scales the pattern into a long strip, it will still return the default rangular texture's rect, it's so strange. From my point of view, the value returned by the get_rect method of control is consistent with intuition. \n\nOn the other hand, if this issue cannot be resolved temporarily due to the compatibility, I think the document description should be more specific at least. I think most users would think that the rect is the orange rect with sprite selected in the 2D editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057150094/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3057169578","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108447#issuecomment-3057169578","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108447","id":3057169578,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62OLSq","user":{"login":"ATho